# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"PDF Arranger merges, splits, rearranges, rotates and crops PDF documents. "
"Everything happens in memory against the pages you can see; nothing is "
"written until you save."
msgstr ""
"PDF Arranger fletter, opdeler, omarrangerer, roterer og beskærer PDF-"
"dokumenter. Alt sker i hukommelsen på de sider, du kan se; intet skrives, "
"før du gemmer."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"It is a front end for pikepdf. Page content is never rewritten — only page "
"order, geometry and composition."
msgstr ""
"Det er en skal omkring pikepdf. Sidernes indhold omskrives aldrig — kun "
"siderækkefølge, geometri og sammensætning."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "Command line"
msgstr "Kommandolinje"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"Files given on the command line are opened as one document. "
"<code>--version</code> prints the version and exits."
msgstr ""
"Filer, der angives på kommandolinjen, åbnes som ét dokument. "
"<code>--version</code> viser versionen og afslutter."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py pdfarranger_qt/mainwindow.py
msgid "Reading"
msgstr "Læsning"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"The application opens in <b>read mode</b>: a continuous page view for "
"reading the document rather than rearranging it. <b>View ▸ Arrange Mode</b> "
"(Ctrl+E) swaps to the thumbnail grid and back."
msgstr ""
"Programmet åbner i <b>læsetilstand</b>: en fortløbende sidevisning til at "
"læse dokumentet frem for at omarrangere det. <b>Visning ▸ "
"Ordningstilstand</b> (Ctrl+E) skifter til miniaturegitteret og tilbage."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"Reading shows the document <i>as edited</i>: rotations, crops, deletions and"
" reordering are all applied, so what you read is what you would get if you "
"saved. Page-editing commands are disabled while reading — bookmarks are the "
"exception, and are edited here and nowhere else."
msgstr ""
"Læsning viser dokumentet <i>som redigeret</i>: rotationer, beskæringer, "
"sletninger og omrokeringer er alle anvendt, så det, du læser, er det, du "
"ville få, hvis du gemte. Sideredigeringskommandoer er slået fra under "
"læsning — bogmærker er undtagelsen og redigeres her og ingen andre steder."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"The page you are on follows you between the two modes. Switching to read "
"mode opens at the page selected in the grid, the first of them if several "
"are selected; switching back scrolls the grid to the page you were reading, "
"without disturbing what you had selected. With nothing selected, reading "
"resumes where you left off — your place in each document is remembered "
"between visits."
msgstr ""
"Den side, du er på, følger dig mellem de to tilstande. At skifte til "
"læsetilstand åbner på den side, der er markeret i gitteret, den første af "
"dem hvis flere er markeret; at skifte tilbage ruller gitteret til den side, "
"du læste, uden at forstyrre det, du havde markeret. Uden markering "
"genoptages læsningen, hvor du slap — din plads i hvert dokument huskes "
"mellem besøgene."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"The toolbar shows which page you are on and how many there are; type a "
"number into it to jump there, or use <b>Ctrl+G</b>."
msgstr ""
"Værktøjslinjen viser, hvilken side du er på, og hvor mange der er; skriv et "
"tal i den for at springe dertil, eller brug <b>Ctrl+G</b>."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>View ▸ Continuous Scroll</b> is on by default; turning it off shows one "
"page at a time. <b>View ▸ Facing Pages</b> puts two pages side by side, the "
"way a book falls open. Both settings are remembered."
msgstr ""
"<b>Visning ▸ Fortløbende rulning</b> er slået til som standard; slår du den "
"fra, vises én side ad gangen. <b>Visning ▸ Opslag</b> stiller to sider side "
"om side, som en bog falder op. Begge indstillinger huskes."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "Moving around a document"
msgstr "At bevæge sig rundt i et dokument"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"One rule for the arrow keys: <b>the modifier decides what moves</b>. Nothing"
" scrolls the view, Option (Alt) moves the text cursor, Shift extends the "
"selection, Command (Ctrl) jumps to an edge, and Fn — Page Up, Page Down, "
"Home and End — jumps further. None of it changes according to whether a text"
" cursor happens to be on the page."
msgstr ""
"Én regel for piletasterne: <b>modifikatortasten afgør, hvad der flytter "
"sig</b>. Ingen ruller visningen, Option (Alt) flytter tekstmarkøren, Skift "
"udvider markeringen, Command (Ctrl) springer til en kant, og Fn — Page Up, "
"Page Down, Home og End — springer længere. Intet af det ændrer sig, alt "
"efter om der tilfældigvis står en tekstmarkør på siden."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "Keys"
msgstr "Taster"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "Continuous"
msgstr "Fortløbende"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py pdfarranger_qt/viewer.py
msgid "One page at a time"
msgstr "Én side ad gangen"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "scroll one line"
msgstr "rul én linje"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "top of the previous / next page"
msgstr "toppen af forrige / næste side"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "previous / next page"
msgstr "forrige / næste side"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "scroll one screen"
msgstr "rul én skærm"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "start / end of the document"
msgstr "dokumentets begyndelse / slutning"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "move the text cursor, by character or line"
msgstr "flyt tekstmarkøren, tegn- eller linjevis"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "extend the selection, by character or line"
msgstr "udvid markeringen, tegn- eller linjevis"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "move the text cursor one word"
msgstr "flyt tekstmarkøren ét ord"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "extend the selection one word"
msgstr "udvid markeringen ét ord"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "cursor to the start / end of the line"
msgstr "markøren til linjens begyndelse / slutning"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "cursor to the start / end of the document"
msgstr "markøren til dokumentets begyndelse / slutning"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"Add Shift to a Command or Option combination to extend the selection instead"
" of moving — <b>Shift+Command+→</b> selects to the end of the line. Adding "
"Option works by the word rather than the character. On Windows and Linux, "
"read Command as Ctrl and Option as Alt; the table is the same everywhere."
msgstr ""
"Føj Skift til en Command- eller Option-kombination for at udvide markeringen"
" frem for at flytte — <b>Skift+Command+→</b> markerer til slutningen af "
"linjen. At tilføje Option arbejder ordvis frem for tegnvis. På Windows og "
"Linux læses Command som Ctrl og Option som Alt; tabellen er den samme "
"overalt."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "Selecting and copying text"
msgstr "At markere og kopiere tekst"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"Drag across the page to select text, across page boundaries if you keep "
"going. <b>Double-click</b> selects a word. <b>Ctrl/Cmd+C</b> copies, "
"<b>Ctrl/Cmd+A</b> selects the text of the page you are on, and <b>Esc</b> "
"clears the selection. The same commands are on the right-click menu."
msgstr ""
"Træk hen over siden for at markere tekst, hen over sidegrænser hvis du "
"fortsætter. <b>Dobbeltklik</b> markerer et ord. <b>Ctrl/Cmd+C</b> kopierer, "
"<b>Ctrl/Cmd+A</b> markerer teksten på den side, du er på, og <b>Esc</b> "
"rydder markeringen. De samme kommandoer findes i højrekliksmenuen."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>Shift+click</b> extends an existing selection to where you clicked. The "
"end you are moving grows out to a whole word, because a single click is an "
"imprecise way to point at one character; the end you started from stays "
"exactly where you put it. Dragging selects by character throughout, since "
"you can watch it and stop where you like."
msgstr ""
"<b>Skift+klik</b> udvider en eksisterende markering til dér, hvor du "
"klikkede. Den ende, du flytter, vokser ud til et helt ord, fordi ét enkelt "
"klik er en upræcis måde at pege på ét tegn; den ende, du startede fra, "
"bliver præcis, hvor du satte den. At trække markerer tegnvis hele vejen, "
"eftersom du kan følge med og stoppe, hvor du vil."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"Clicking on text leaves a blinking <b>text cursor</b>. That is what "
"Shift+arrow extends from, and what the Option and Command combinations above"
" move. It stays where you put it — scrolling, paging and clicking off the "
"page all leave it alone — until you press Esc or open another document."
msgstr ""
"At klikke på tekst efterlader en blinkende <b>tekstmarkør</b>. Det er den, "
"Skift+pil udvider fra, og den, som Option- og Command-kombinationerne "
"ovenfor flytter. Den bliver, hvor du satte den — rulning, sideskift og klik "
"uden for siden lader den være — indtil du trykker Esc eller åbner et andet "
"dokument."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "Following links"
msgstr "At følge links"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"Click a link to follow it. Links to a page in the same document jump there; "
"links to the web open in your browser. Hovering over one shows where it "
"goes, which is worth reading before you click: many links in a PDF are not "
"written by its author at all but inferred from the text, so what a link "
"points at is not always what the words appear to say."
msgstr ""
"Klik på et link for at følge det. Links til en side i samme dokument "
"springer dertil; links til nettet åbnes i din browser. At holde markøren "
"over et viser, hvor det fører hen, og det er værd at læse, før du klikker: "
"mange links i en PDF er slet ikke skrevet af forfatteren, men udledt af "
"teksten, så hvad et link peger på, er ikke altid det, ordene ser ud til at "
"sige."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"Only ordinary web and mail links are handed to the system — http, https, "
"mailto and ftp. A document is a file that arrived from somewhere, and "
"anything else it asks to open is refused and reported rather than acted on."
msgstr ""
"Kun almindelige web- og e-mail-links overdrages til systemet — http, https, "
"mailto og ftp. Et dokument er en fil, der er kommet et sted fra, og alt "
"andet, det beder om at åbne, afvises og rapporteres frem for at blive "
"udført."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "Right-clicking a link offers <b>Open Link</b> and <b>Copy Link Address</b>."
msgstr "Højreklik på et link giver <b>Åbn link</b> og <b>Kopiér linkadresse</b>."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "Bookmarks"
msgstr "Bogmærker"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"The sidebar shows the document's bookmarks. Click one to jump to it. "
"Everything below is on the sidebar's right-click menu, and every command can"
" be undone."
msgstr ""
"Sidepanelet viser dokumentets bogmærker. Klik på et for at springe dertil. "
"Alt nedenfor findes i sidepanelets højrekliksmenu, og hver kommando kan "
"fortrydes."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>Add Bookmark Here</b> makes one pointing at the page you are reading, "
"named after whatever text you have selected — so select a heading, then add."
" With nothing selected it is named after the page. <b>Add Child Bookmark "
"Here</b> does the same, nested under the entry you clicked."
msgstr ""
"<b>Tilføj bogmærke her</b> laver et, der peger på den side, du læser, "
"opkaldt efter den tekst, du har markeret — markér altså en overskrift, og "
"tilføj så. Uden markering opkaldes det efter siden. <b>Tilføj underbogmærke "
"her</b> gør det samme, indlejret under den post, du klikkede på."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>Rename</b> edits the title in place. <b>Re-home to This Page</b> points "
"an existing bookmark at the page you are on, keeping its title. "
"<b>Delete</b> removes an entry and <i>promotes</i> its children into its "
"place; <b>Delete with Children</b> removes the whole branch."
msgstr ""
"<b>Omdøb</b> retter titlen på stedet. <b>Peg om til denne side</b> får et "
"eksisterende bogmærke til at pege på den side, du er på, med titlen bevaret."
" <b>Slet</b> fjerner en post og <i>rykker</i> dens underpunkter op i dens "
"sted; <b>Slet med underpunkter</b> fjerner hele grenen."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"Drag entries within the sidebar to re-nest or reorder them. <b>Expand All "
"Children</b> and <b>Collapse All Children</b> open or shut a whole branch at"
" once."
msgstr ""
"Træk poster inden for sidepanelet for at indlejre eller omrokere dem. "
"<b>Udfold alle underpunkter</b> og <b>Fold alle underpunkter sammen</b> "
"åbner eller lukker en hel gren på én gang."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>Style</b> sets a bookmark bold or italic, or gives it a colour, as the "
"tree shows."
msgstr ""
"<b>Stil</b> gør et bogmærke fedt eller kursivt, eller giver det en farve, "
"som træet viser."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"A bookmark whose page has been deleted is <b>greyed out</b> rather than "
"removed: its title may still be worth keeping, and you can point it "
"somewhere else with Re-home. Undoing the deletion reconnects it. <b>Delete "
"Dangling Bookmarks</b> clears them all out; it leaves alone any entry that "
"points nowhere on purpose, which is a legitimate way to write a heading."
msgstr ""
"Et bogmærke, hvis side er slettet, bliver <b>gråtonet</b> frem for fjernet: "
"dets titel kan stadig være værd at beholde, og du kan pege det et andet sted"
" hen med Peg om. At fortryde sletningen forbinder det igen. <b>Slet løse "
"bogmærker</b> rydder dem alle væk; det lader enhver post være, der med vilje"
" peger ingen steder hen, hvilket er en helt legitim måde at skrive en "
"overskrift på."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"Bookmark edits are part of the document and are written when you save, along"
" with each entry's colour and style and which branches are left open. The "
"one thing that cannot be saved is a bookmark with no page: there is no way "
"to record “points at a page that is gone”, so it comes back as a heading "
"with its title intact."
msgstr ""
"Bogmærkeændringer er en del af dokumentet og skrives, når du gemmer, sammen "
"med hver posts farve og stil og hvilke grene der efterlades åbne. Det "
"eneste, der ikke kan gemmes, er et bogmærke uden side: der er ingen måde at "
"notere ”peger på en side, der er væk”, så det kommer tilbage som en "
"overskrift med titlen intakt."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "Arranging pages"
msgstr "At ordne sider"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"Drag pages to reorder them. Hold <b>Ctrl</b> while dropping to copy instead "
"of move."
msgstr ""
"Træk sider for at omrokere dem. Hold <b>Ctrl</b> nede, mens du slipper, for "
"at kopiere frem for at flytte."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"Drag pages onto another window of the application to copy them there, or use"
" ordinary copy and paste."
msgstr ""
"Træk sider over på et andet af programmets vinduer for at kopiere dem "
"dertil, eller brug almindelig kopiér og indsæt."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>Paste As Odd/Even Pages</b> interleaves the clipboard with the document —"
" this is how two single-sided scans of a double-sided original are "
"recombined. If the second scan came off a duplex feeder it will be in "
"reverse order; use <b>Arrange ▸ Reverse Order</b> on it first."
msgstr ""
"<b>Indsæt som ulige/lige sider</b> fletter udklipsholderen ind i dokumentet "
"— sådan sættes to enkeltsidede scanninger af et dobbeltsidet original sammen"
" igen. Kom den anden scanning fra en duplexføder, ligger den i omvendt "
"rækkefølge; brug <b>Ordn ▸ Omvendt rækkefølge</b> på den først."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"To move pages a long way, use <b>Move to Start</b>, <b>Move to End</b> or "
"<b>Move to Page…</b> rather than dragging — in a long document the far end "
"is a great deal of scrolling away. They are on the Edit menu and on the "
"right-click menu, and <b>Move to Page…</b> asks for the number the page "
"should <i>become</i>."
msgstr ""
"For at flytte sider langt bruger du <b>Flyt til begyndelsen</b>, <b>Flyt til"
" slutningen</b> eller <b>Flyt til side…</b> frem for at trække — i et langt "
"dokument ligger den anden ende rigtig meget rulning væk. De findes i menuen "
"Redigér og i højrekliksmenuen, og <b>Flyt til side…</b> spørger om det "
"nummer, siden skal <i>blive</i>."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"Prefer these to cut and paste for moving. A pasted page is a <i>new</i> page"
" as far as the document is concerned, so any bookmarks pointing at the "
"original are left behind with nowhere to go. Moving keeps the page itself, "
"and its bookmarks come with it."
msgstr ""
"Foretræk disse frem for klip og indsæt, når du flytter. En indsat side er en"
" <i>ny</i> side, set fra dokumentet, så bogmærker, der pegede på originalen,"
" bliver efterladt uden noget sted at pege hen. At flytte bevarer selve "
"siden, og dens bogmærker følger med."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "Stamping and tiling"
msgstr "At stemple og samle"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>Page ▸ Add Page Numbers…</b> and <b>Page ▸ Add Watermark…</b> draw text "
"onto the selected pages. Both add a <i>layer</i> rather than rewriting the "
"page, so both can be undone and neither touches the file you opened."
msgstr ""
"<b>Side ▸ Tilføj sidetal…</b> og <b>Side ▸ Tilføj vandmærke…</b> tegner "
"tekst på de markerede sider. Begge tilføjer et <i>lag</i> frem for at "
"omskrive siden, så begge kan fortrydes, og ingen af dem rører den fil, du "
"åbnede."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Page numbers follow the arrangement, not the source document: they are "
"numbered in the order the pages are in now. <code>{n}</code> in the format "
"is the page number and <code>{total}</code> the number of pages, so "
"<code>Page {n} of {total}</code> does what it looks like."
msgstr ""
"Sidetallene følger ordningen, ikke kildedokumentet: de nummereres i den "
"rækkefølge, siderne ligger i nu. <code>{n}</code> i formatet er sidetallet "
"og <code>{total}</code> antallet af sider, så <code>Side {n} af "
"{total}</code> gør det, det ser ud til."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>Arrange ▸ Pages per Sheet…</b> tiles several pages onto one, in reading "
"order — the printer's <i>N-up</i>. The sheet turns sideways when that lets "
"the pages come out larger, which is why two-up gives a landscape sheet and "
"four-up does not."
msgstr ""
"<b>Ordn ▸ Sider pr. ark…</b> lægger flere sider på én, i læserækkefølge — "
"trykkeriets <i>N-up</i>. Arket vendes på tværs, når siderne derved bliver "
"større, og derfor giver to pr. ark et liggende ark, mens fire pr. ark ikke "
"gør."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "Saving a document"
msgstr "At gemme et dokument"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>Optimize for the web</b> in Preferences lays the saved file out so a "
"browser can show the first page before the rest has arrived. <b>Compress</b>"
" repacks its streams and objects; how much that saves depends entirely on "
"the file, and one full of photographs will barely move."
msgstr ""
"<b>Optimér til nettet</b> i Præferencer lægger den gemte fil op, så en "
"browser kan vise første side, før resten er nået frem. <b>Komprimér</b> "
"pakker dens strømme og objekter om; hvor meget det sparer, afhænger helt af "
"filen, og en fil fuld af fotografier rykker sig knap nok."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>File ▸ Remove All Metadata</b> is a switch, like Password: turn it on and"
" the next save writes a document with no title, no author and no record of "
"what produced it. Edit Properties greys out while it is on, because there "
"would be nothing to edit."
msgstr ""
"<b>Fil ▸ Fjern alle metadata</b> er en kontakt, ligesom Adgangskode: slå den"
" til, og næste gemning skriver et dokument uden titel, uden forfatter og "
"uden spor af, hvad der frembragte det. Rediger egenskaber bliver gråtonet, "
"mens den er slået til, fordi der så ikke ville være noget at redigere."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>File ▸ Viewer Preferences…</b> is how the saved document asks a reader to"
" open it — with the bookmarks showing, two pages at a time, and so on. "
"Readers are free to ignore all of it. The settings are read from the file "
"you opened, so a document that already had them keeps them."
msgstr ""
"<b>Fil ▸ Fremviserindstillinger…</b> er den måde, det gemte dokument beder "
"en læser om at åbne det på — med bogmærkerne fremme, to sider ad gangen, og "
"så videre. Læsere må gerne ignorere alt det. Indstillingerne læses fra den "
"fil, du åbnede, så et dokument, der allerede havde dem, beholder dem."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>File ▸ Repair Document…</b> rebuilds a damaged PDF. It works on a file "
"you pick rather than the one on screen, because the file worth repairing is "
"usually one this application cannot open properly either. It reports what it"
" found before writing anything."
msgstr ""
"<b>Fil ▸ Reparér dokument…</b> genopbygger en beskadiget PDF. Det arbejder "
"på en fil, du vælger, frem for den på skærmen, fordi den fil, der er værd at"
" reparere, som regel er en, dette program heller ikke kan åbne ordentligt. "
"Det rapporterer, hvad det fandt, før der skrives noget."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "Mouse"
msgstr "Mus"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "<b>Ctrl + scroll</b> — zoom"
msgstr "<b>Ctrl + rul</b> — zoom"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "<b>Shift + scroll</b> — scroll sideways"
msgstr "<b>Skift + rul</b> — rul sidelæns"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "<b>Alt + scroll</b> — scroll exactly one row"
msgstr "<b>Alt + rul</b> — rul præcis én række"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "<b>Double-click</b> — fit the page to the window, and back"
msgstr "<b>Dobbeltklik</b> — tilpas siden til vinduet, og tilbage"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>Click and drag</b> on empty space — rubber-band select; keep scrolling to"
" extend it"
msgstr ""
"<b>Klik og træk</b> på tom plads — markér med elastikramme; bliv ved med at "
"rulle for at udvide den"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "Moving around the grid"
msgstr "At bevæge sig rundt i gitteret"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>Arrow keys</b> move between pages, <b>Page Up</b> and <b>Page Down</b> "
"move a screenful at a time, and <b>Home</b> and <b>End</b> jump to the first"
" and last page. Hold <b>Shift</b> with any of them to extend the selection."
msgstr ""
"<b>Piletasterne</b> flytter mellem sider, <b>Page Up</b> og <b>Page Down</b>"
" flytter en skærmfuld ad gangen, og <b>Home</b> og <b>End</b> springer til "
"første og sidste side. Hold <b>Skift</b> nede sammen med en af dem for at "
"udvide markeringen."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>Fit One Page</b> (F) scales so a whole page fits in the window and shows "
"one page per row — use it to work on a single page at a time. <b>Fit "
"Multiple Pages</b> (Shift+M) uses the same scale but lets as many pages sit "
"side by side as the window takes. <b>Fit Width</b> (Shift+F) fills the "
"window across instead, which shows the page wider but taller than the "
"window. Double-clicking the grid toggles Fit One Page on and off."
msgstr ""
"<b>Tilpas én side</b> (F) skalerer, så en hel side er i vinduet, og viser én"
" side pr. række — brug det til at arbejde med én side ad gangen. <b>Tilpas "
"flere sider</b> (Skift+M) bruger samme skala, men lader lige så mange sider "
"stå side om side, som vinduet kan rumme. <b>Tilpas til bredden</b> (Skift+F)"
" fylder vinduet på tværs i stedet, hvilket viser siden bredere, men højere "
"end vinduet. Dobbeltklik i gitteret slår Tilpas én side til og fra."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"With pages selected, all three fit the selection rather than the whole "
"document."
msgstr ""
"Med sider markeret tilpasser alle tre efter markeringen frem for hele "
"dokumentet."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "Finding text"
msgstr "At finde tekst"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>Find</b> selects the pages that contain the phrase and boxes each hit on "
"the thumbnail, so you can see where on the page it is. The boxes clear as "
"soon as you change the document, since the pages they were drawn for may "
"have moved."
msgstr ""
"<b>Find</b> markerer de sider, der indeholder udtrykket, og rammer hvert "
"træf ind på miniaturen, så du kan se, hvor på siden det er. Rammerne "
"forsvinder, så snart du ændrer dokumentet, da de sider, de blev tegnet for, "
"kan have flyttet sig."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"Every shortcut can be changed in <b>Edit ▸ Preferences ▸ Keyboard "
"shortcuts</b>, where they are listed under the menu each one belongs to."
msgstr ""
"Hver genvej kan ændres i <b>Redigér ▸ Præferencer ▸ Tastaturgenveje</b>, "
"hvor de er opført under den menu, hver enkelt hører til."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid "Passwords"
msgstr "Adgangskoder"

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"Opening an encrypted document asks for its password, which is remembered "
"until the document is closed."
msgstr ""
"At åbne et krypteret dokument beder om dets adgangskode, som huskes, indtil "
"dokumentet lukkes."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>File ▸ Password</b> encrypts the document when it is next saved. It is a "
"switch: turn it on and you are asked for a password, turn it off and the "
"next save is unencrypted. The password is never written to your settings, so"
" it applies to this session only — and if you forget it, the file cannot be "
"recovered."
msgstr ""
"<b>Fil ▸ Adgangskode</b> krypterer dokumentet, næste gang det gemmes. Det er"
" en kontakt: slå den til, og du bliver bedt om en adgangskode, slå den fra, "
"og næste gemning er ukrypteret. Adgangskoden skrives aldrig til dine "
"indstillinger, så den gælder kun denne session — og glemmer du den, kan "
"filen ikke genskabes."

# machine translation, unreviewed
#: pdfarranger_qt/dialogs.py
msgid ""
"<b>File ▸ Unlock</b> goes the other way: open the document with its "
"password, choose Unlock, and the next save writes it without one. It is only"
" available when there is encryption to remove."
msgstr ""
"<b>Fil ▸ Lås op</b> går den anden vej: åbn dokumentet med dets adgangskode, "
"vælg Lås op, og næste gemning skriver det uden. Kun tilgængelig, når der er "
"kryptering at fjerne."

# machine translation, unreviewed
